{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/258097-how-airtight-is-a-death-cycle","id":258097,"title":"How \"Airtight\" is a Death Cycle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-16T07:21:52-07:00","id":258097,"title":"How \"Airtight\" is a Death Cycle?","content":"So when a mummy is killed mid-Descent, they fall into Neter-Khertet and go through a death-cycle, where they experience a figurative tunnel back to their body, with manifestations of memories both recalled and forgotten. Elsewhere in the Mummy core book, Neter-Khertet is described as what mummies call Twilight. And everywhere else Twilight is described, the books concerned take pains to point out it's not another dimension, but the condition of being invisible and incorporeal in this world.<br /> <br /> Ergo: a death cycle would seem to be an incporeal &quot;construct&quot; cented on where the mummy died, and the location of her body if that ends up different.<br /> <br /> So how &quot;airtight&quot; is this construct? Can another entity in Twilight - a ghost, a spirit, an astrally projecting vampire or mage - stumble into it? And what are the implications for them or the mummy if they do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T10:10:35-07:00","id":258255,"title":"","content":"I'd have to give the book a thorough reread but my gut tells me it's airtight, unless you need it to not be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/252-basketcase","name":"basketcase","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar252_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T16:15:58-07:00","id":258520,"title":"","content":"My initial reading was that, while the Mummy is in Twilight (isn't this spoiler GM information) it does seem like a limited, 'constructed' experience for the Arisen. If a Mage or Werewolf were stumbling through Twilight and encountered the Arisen - which would be strange enough by all accounts - I think they would see them acting as if they were walking through and interacting with <i>another</i> dimension rather than just the one they're expected to be in (as in, Twilight)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}